+
+# Manage NFC Readers
+
+Use the station's HTTPS management address and its assigned administrator username and password. These credentials are separate from your member-portal login. Only operators responsible for access equipment should have them.
+
+## Configure a station
+
+Open **Configuration**, enter a unique **Device name**, and select its **Role**. Door opens for 10 seconds, garagedoor for 30, test for 9, and latch for 5. Tool toggles on each accepted scan and needs the configured **Tool ID** plus a current checkout for that tool.
+
+Stop the relay before changing settings. **Save and synchronize** must reach the server before the change is applied. If the server rejects the change or is unavailable, correct the problem and save again.
+
+## Enroll an assigned fob
+
+First assign the fob to the correct member through the normal member-portal workflow. On a supervised station, check **Enrollment station**, then choose **Save and synchronize**.
+
+Hold the assigned fob at the reader until feedback appears. The station provisions its protected credential and verifies it before recording enrollment. An unknown fob is rejected and left untouched. Enrollment does not make an expired, lost, revoked or otherwise ineligible membership valid.
+
+After enrollment, choose **Disable enrollment locally now**. This works even when the network is unavailable. A failed or interrupted enrollment may be retried at an enabled station; ask an access-system maintainer to inspect a fob that repeatedly fails. Do not repeatedly rewrite an unrelated or nonblank fob.
+
+## Inspect the reader
+
+**Statistics** shows network/API/MQTT/NFC state, clock trust, relay state, memory and audit-loss counters. A clock that cannot be trusted prevents admission. A production security configuration that is not ready also prevents admission.
+
+**cacheKeyReady** must be true before scans are enabled. If it is false or configuration reports **Cache key unavailable; restore configuration and restart**, record **lastError** and contact the access-system maintainer. Keep NVS and flash intact: deleting a key can make cached cards and unsent records unreadable. The maintainer must restore the original configuration/state or deliberately reprovision the device, then restart it. Management pages remain available during this fault.
+
+**Cards** searches the local cache by UID or holder. FirstScan is the first recorded presentation at this station, expressed in epoch milliseconds. **Never scanned** means no presentation was recorded; **Time unavailable** means the presentation occurred without a recoverable timestamp. Card keys are never shown.
+
+**Checkouts** lists cached grants for a tool station. An active membership alone does not authorize a tool. The member also needs a current checkout, and the tool and shop must be available.
+
+## Update firmware
+
+With the relay off, open **Update** and select the maintainer-provided signed firmware image. The reader disables access during the update and reboots after success. Filesystem uploads are not supported because they would replace the local cache and unsent activity records.
+
+Keep power connected. After reboot, check **Statistics**, the station name/role, cached FirstScan values and a supervised test scan. Contact the maintainer if the previous firmware returns or the new firmware does not become healthy.
+
+## Network outages
+
+A reader can use an already cached, authenticated, unexpired card while offline. It cannot learn a new revocation until connectivity returns. New or unenrolled cards require a server connection. Activity records wait in flash and retry automatically; **auditLoss** means records were lost because of storage failure or spool overflow.
+
+Report the station name, approximate time and displayed rejection to the maintainer. Do not clear flash or reset credentials as a troubleshooting shortcut.
